{"packet_id":"D043-02","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Resident Protections Ordinance relocation amounts for demolition of lower income households","requirement":"When lower income households are displaced by demolition of their units for new construction, the landlord must pay standardized relocation amounts: $115,480 (extremely low income), $96,750 (very low income) or $87,450 (low income).","key_value":"$115,480 extremely low; $96,750 very low; $87,450 low income (2026-07-01 to 2027-06-30)","coverage_conditions":"Only Low, Very Low and Extremely Low income households displaced from RPO-covered units demolished for new construction where the owner replaces the units.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Resident Protections Ordinance units demolished for new construction"},"exemptions":"Households above low income receive Chart A (RSO or JCO) amounts instead of these standardized payments.","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2026-07-01","citation":"Resident Protections Ordinance (RPO)","quoted_span":"CHART B: Resident Protections Ordinance Standardized Payments
