{"packet_id":"D043-02","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Timing and allocation of relocation assistance payments","requirement":"Relocation assistance must be made available within 15 days of service of the written notice of eviction; a sole tenant receives the entire payment, multiple tenants share pro rata, the higher applicable amount is paid per unit, and the landlord may instead use an escrow account at its own cost.","key_value":"15 days from service of written notice of eviction","coverage_conditions":"All landlords required to provide relocation assistance to tenants under City ordinances, including those choosing to pay through an escrow account.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Rental units subject to City relocation assistance requirements"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"RAC Regulations § 960.00","quoted_span":"4. Payments shall be made available within fifteen (15) days of service of the written notice of eviction; however, the landlord may, at the landlord's sole discretion and at the landlord's cost, elect to pay the monetary relocation benefits through an escrow account.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.7,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D043-02","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Rent offset against relocation assistance","requirement":"A landlord may offset a tenant's accumulated rent against any relocation assistance, except where the relocation is owed because a governmental agency order requires the tenant to vacate or comply for an unpermitted dwelling.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Landlords owing relocation assistance to tenants under the City ordinances; the offset is available on the stated terms.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":"No offset where termination is required by a governmental agency order to vacate or comply for an unpermitted dwelling.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"L.A. Mun. Code § 151.09","quoted_span":"Relocation Offset: A landlord may offset the tenant's accumulated rent against any relocation assistance, unless the relocation assistance is owed because a termination of tenancy is required by a governmental agency order to vacate or comply issued for an unpermitted dwelling. (LAMC 151.09.G,5., 165.06.J.).","interaction":null,"confidence":0.7,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D043-02","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Tenant remedy for non-payment of relocation assistance","requirement":"A tenant may raise the landlord's failure to provide relocation assistance as an affirmative defense in an eviction action and may file a complaint with LAHD; escrow disputes must be noticed to LAHD by the escrow holder.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Tenants in rental units where the landlord owes relocation assistance but has not paid it.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"Tenant may raise non-payment as an affirmative defense to the landlord's action to recover possession, may file a LAHD complaint, and may seek a private right of action with legal advice.","effective_date":null,"citation":"RAC Regulations § 967.00","quoted_span":"Non-payment Dispute - In an action by the landlord to recover possession of a rental unit, the tenant may raise as an affirmative defense the failure of the landlord to provide relocation assistance.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.7,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D043-02","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"One month's rent relocation for JCO single-family dwellings owned by natural persons","requirement":"When a JCO single-family dwelling is owned by a qualifying natural person, relocation assistance is one month's rent in effect when the written notice to terminate was served, paid as a monetary payment or credit.","key_value":"1 month's rent","coverage_conditions":"JCO single-family dwelling; owner is a natural person, including a trust or legal entity controlled by that natural person, owning no more than four dwelling units and a single-family home on a separate lot in Los Angeles.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":4,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Single-family dwelling subject to the JCO owned by a natural person"},"exemptions":"Los Angeles Municipal Code Section 151.30(E) shall not apply.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"L.A. Mun. Code § 165.06","quoted_span":"who owns no more than four dwelling units and a single-family home on a separate lot in the City of Los Angeles: one month’s rent that was in effect when the landlord served the written notice to terminate the tenancy, as either a monetary payment or credit.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.7,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
